course: dictionary
lesson: 89
title: Ada: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Ada was the daughter of the poet Lord Byron.» A daughter is a person, so here Ada is a girl's name.
explain: The same word can name something else. «The Ada programming language was created in the late 1970s and early 1980s.» Here Ada is a language people use to give instructions to computers, and it is named after Ada Lovelace.
explain: Capital letters and signs help too. «ADA» on US signs is short for the Americans with Disabilities Act, a law about ramps and lifts for disabled people. Always ask: does the sentence talk about a person, a language, or a sign?
fact: Ada is a girl's name. It is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Ada Lovelace was an English mathematician who wrote what is often called the first computer program.
fact: Ada is also a programming language, named after Ada Lovelace.
fact: ADA stands for the Americans with Disabilities Act, a law that protects disabled people.
fact: Ada Lovelace Day, on the second Tuesday of October, celebrates women in science, technology, engineering and maths. It started in 2009.
exercise: «Ada was the daughter of the poet Lord Byron.» In this sentence, what is Ada? | A road sign | *A girl's name | A computer language | A type of poem
exercise: «The Ada programming language was created in the late 1970s.» What is Ada in this sentence? | A law about disabled people | A girl's name | *A computer language | A kind of ramp
exercise: On a US sign, ADA stands for what? | A programming language | *The Americans with Disabilities Act | A famous mathematician
test: Ada Lovelace is remembered for writing what is often called the first what? | *Computer program | Road sign | Ramp for wheelchairs | Poem by Lord Byron
test: Why does Ada start with a capital letter when it is a name? | Because it is always the first word in a book | *Because it names one special person or thing | Because it is a long word | Because it is a verb
exam: «Ada's so relieved she can't even speak; she just nods and runs.» In this story, what is Ada? | A mathematician's notebook | *A character's name in a story | A computer language | A law about disabled people
